<BaseLayout
  title="Pool Deck & Patio Power Washing in Kissimmee | Go Pro Guide"
  description="Clean algae, mold & grime from pool decks and patios in Kissimmee. Concrete, pavers, travertine. Pressure vs soft wash. Cost & process."
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pool-deck-power-washing-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "Pool Deck & Patio Power Washing in Kissimmee",
        "description": "How to clean algae, mold, and grime from pool decks and patios in Kissimmee. Cost, process, and when to use pressure wash vs soft wash.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pool-deck-power-washing-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Pool Deck Power Washing",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pool-deck-power-washing-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Pool Deck Power Washing</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Pool Deck & Patio Power Washing in Kissimmee</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Remove algae, mold & slippery grime from pool decks & patios. Concrete, pavers, travertine. Safe & effective cleaning.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Pool decks and patios in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida get slippery fast—algae, mold, mildew, and dirt buildup from humidity, splashing water, and afternoon rain. <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Power washing</a> removes the grime, restores grip, and makes outdoor spaces safe and clean again.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Why Pool Decks & Patios Get Slippery in Florida</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            Florida's heat, humidity, and frequent rain create perfect conditions for algae and mold. Pool decks stay damp from splashing water and humidity—algae grows fast. Patios shaded by trees or screen enclosures stay damp longer, breeding mildew.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Algae and mold make surfaces slippery—dangerous around pools where kids run and jump. Green or black algae on concrete pavers or travertine isn't just ugly; it's a slip hazard. Power washing removes it and restores traction.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Pressure Wash vs Soft Wash: Which for Pool Decks?</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Pressure Wash for Most Pool Decks</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Use on:</strong> Concrete, concrete pavers, brick pavers (non-sealed or factory-sealed)<br />
            <strong>Pressure:</strong> 2,500-3,500 PSI<br />
            <strong>Why:</strong> High pressure blasts away algae, dirt, and embedded grime from porous concrete.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Most pool decks in Kissimmee are concrete or concrete pavers. Pressure washing removes algae, dirt, and the slippery biofilm that builds up in Florida humidity. We use a surface cleaner attachment (spinning nozzles under a hood) that cleans evenly without streaking or tiger-striping.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Soft Wash for Delicate Surfaces</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Use on:</strong> Travertine, natural stone, sealed pavers, wood decks<br />
            <strong>Pressure:</strong> Low (500-1,000 PSI) + cleaning solution<br />
            <strong>Why:</strong> Prevents etching, pitting, or seal damage on softer/sealed surfaces.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Travertine and natural stone are softer than concrete—high pressure can etch or pit the surface. Sealed pavers can lose their seal under high pressure. For these surfaces, we use <a href="/guides/soft-wash-vs-pressure-wash-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">soft wash</a>: low pressure + algaecide/mildew remover solution. The chemical does the work, not the pressure.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How We Clean Pool Decks & Patios</h2>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 mb-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Pre-wet surrounding plants:</strong> Water protects landscaping from cleaning runoff.</li>
            <li><strong>Apply cleaning solution (if needed):</strong> For heavy algae or mildew, we pre-treat with algaecide or mildew remover. Let it sit 10-15 minutes to break down growth.</li>
            <li><strong>Pressure wash or soft wash:</strong> Use appropriate method for the surface type. Surface cleaner for large flat areas (even cleaning, no streaks). Wand for edges, corners, and around pool coping.</li>
            <li><strong>Rinse thoroughly:</strong> Remove all cleaning solution and loosened grime.</li>
            <li><strong>Post-rinse plants:</strong> Final rinse of landscaping to wash away any chemical residue.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Pool Deck & Patio Materials in Kissimmee</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Concrete (Poured or Stamped)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Cleaning method:</strong> Pressure wash<br />
            <strong>Cost:</strong> $100-$300 for typical pool deck<br />
            <strong>Notes:</strong> Concrete is porous and holds algae. Pressure washing blasts it clean. Stamped concrete (decorative patterns) can handle pressure but avoid etching the surface—don't hold the nozzle too close.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Concrete Pavers</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Cleaning method:</strong> Pressure wash<br />
            <strong>Cost:</strong> $150-$400 for typical pool deck<br />
            <strong>Notes:</strong> Pavers have grout joints that fill with dirt and algae. Pressure washing cleans the pavers and joints. After cleaning, you can re-sand joints and seal pavers (optional—sealing reduces future algae growth).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Travertine</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Cleaning method:</strong> Soft wash<br />
            <strong>Cost:</strong> $200-$500 for typical pool deck<br />
            <strong>Notes:</strong> Travertine is natural limestone—soft, porous, and prone to etching. Use low pressure + cleaning solution. Never use high-pressure directly on travertine or it pits and damages.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Brick Pavers</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Cleaning method:</strong> Pressure wash<br />
            <strong>Cost:</strong> $150-$350 for typical patio<br />
            <strong>Notes:</strong> Brick pavers handle pressure well. Clean like concrete pavers—blast away algae and dirt from surface and joints.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Often to Power Wash Pool Decks in Kissimmee</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Annually:</strong> Minimum for most homes. Algae, mold, and dirt build up over a year.<br />
            <strong>Twice a year:</strong> If your pool is heavily used, shaded, or near trees. More traffic and shade = faster algae growth.<br />
            <strong>Before selling:</strong> Clean pool deck before listing photos—buyers notice slippery, stained decks.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Kissimmee vacation rental owners often power wash pool decks every 6 months to keep outdoor spaces guest-ready and avoid slip complaints.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Our take:</strong> Pool decks and patios are safety zones—slippery surfaces cause falls. Power washing removes algae and mold, restores traction, and makes outdoor spaces safe again. In Central Florida's humid climate, annual cleaning is essential. Don't wait until someone slips.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Power Washing Cost for Pool Decks & Patios</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Small patio or pool deck (200-400 sq ft):</strong> $100-$200<br />
            <strong>Medium pool deck (400-800 sq ft):</strong> $150-$350<br />
            <strong>Large pool deck or full patio (800-1,200 sq ft):</strong> $250-$500
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Pricing depends on surface area, material type (travertine costs more than concrete), and buildup severity. See <a href="/guides/pressure-washing-cost-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">full power washing cost guide</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Questions</h2>
          
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Will power washing damage my pool deck?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                No, if done correctly. Concrete and concrete pavers handle high pressure. Travertine and sealed pavers need soft wash (low pressure). We use the right method for each surface.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Can you power wash around the pool without draining it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Yes. We clean around pools while they're full. We direct runoff away from the pool and avoid spraying water directly into it. Cleaning solution is diluted and rinses away—no pool chemistry issues.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">How long does it take to power wash a pool deck?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Small deck: 1-2 hours. Large deck or full patio: 2-4 hours. Depends on size, buildup severity, and material type.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Should I seal my pavers after power washing?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Optional but helpful. Sealing pavers makes them easier to clean, reduces algae growth, and enhances color. We can seal after cleaning (extra cost). Seal lasts 2-3 years in Florida.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Pool decks and patios get slippery from algae, mold, and grime in Central Florida's humid climate. Power washing removes buildup, restores traction, and keeps outdoor spaces safe. Use pressure wash for concrete and pavers, soft wash for travertine and sealed surfaces. Clean annually minimum—more often for heavily used pools or vacation rentals. Cost $100-$500 depending on size and material.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Pool Deck or Patio Cleaning?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              We power wash pool decks and patios in Kissimmee, Orlando, and Central Florida. Free estimates. Safe cleaning for all surface types.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Professional Pool Deck & Patio Cleaning"
    description="Remove algae & slippery grime. Safe for all surfaces. Serving Kissimmee, Orlando & Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
